 "section_summary": "This section contains pages from the April 1, 1936 edition of The Vancouver Sun reproducing an address and multi-part article by publisher Robert Cromie titled 'The Modernization of Asia' ('Asia Is Doubling Living Standards'). Drawing on his extensive tour across Hawaii, Samoa, New Zealand, Australia, New Guinea, the Philippines, China, and Japan, Cromie argues that the rapid industrialization and demographic surge of Asia represent the central historical movement of the era, eclipsing European affairs and the Great Depression. He examines social and political developments across the Orient, including China's modernization under Chiang Kai-shek and the repercussions of military assassinations in Tokyo, urging Western Canada and the Pacific Coast to seize burgeoning transpacific trade opportunities.",
